= Automated market maker — Technical =

A constant-function market maker maintains a trading function φ(x) over reserves x and accepts trades that preserve or satisfy a rule derived from φ after fees. The local gradient of the invariant induces marginal exchange rates. Other AMMs may use dynamic weights, ranges, curves, auctions, or hybrid mechanisms.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* AMM ≠ constant-product market maker only
* AMM ≠ liquidity pool by identity
* algorithmic quote ≠ externally correct price

